#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157167 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157352 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "109b0bfb-10fe-5b31-adb2-be746ef71936" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Using a Table of Values"}] :question/id #uuid "dfd30d6a-23f2-5304-8cb1-cc3a0f31463e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7820" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x= \\dfrac{1}{2}y - \\sqrt y\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}y = 0 & ⟶x = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0 - \\sqrt{0} = 0 \\\\ y = 1 & ⟶x = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 - \\sqrt{1} =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y = 4 & ⟶x = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 - \\sqrt{4} = 0 \\\\ y = 16 & ⟶x = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 16 - \\sqrt{16} = 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\dfrac12$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(0,0), \\quad \\left(-\\dfrac 12,1\\right), \\quad (0,4), \\quad (4,16)\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/70/709bfcd1e69a0e4fd88d95fb9d8592de93921fad230b5f892059525871dc50fb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157168 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157353 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51ae30bd-569c-52dd-96a0-4244578db5bf" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting X as a Function of Y Given the Graph of the Corresponding Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1a638e6a-e5ab-5a60-81f5-2847e917b456" :question/math-academy-id "e-7821" :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Sketch the graph of $x=f(y)$.\n\n![](images/76/76268e0ba23b56af4c7215a4a44f459e6a3ea42454f53df1d39894df16513865.png)" :question/worked-solution "To plot the graph of $x=f(y)$, we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and reflect it over the line $y=x$, as follows:\n\n![](images/2e/2e11bec1e27fd59a1b4ea4e44070591acf5cd8fefebe6d5e1a46ef0be3f5129f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157169 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157354 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2981f6-bfbf-5c1e-a4a2-2814dc24804a" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Quadratic Function Where X Is a Function of Y"}] :question/id #uuid "e6282f0a-7891-5261-968e-63aa42421d00" :question/math-academy-id "e-7822" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x=-2y^2 - 3y$." :question/worked-solution "To plot $x=-2y^2-3y$, we will first plot the function $y=-2x^2-3x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x$.\n\nThe curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny = -x(2x+3)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we see that we have a negative parabola with roots at $x=0$ and\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac32\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/c2/c2a1492655ff33a49bd21e911b13b99d67191a4cd39683f34fca4be295dda41a.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=-2y^2-3y$, we just have to reflect the curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ over the line $y=x$, as follows:\n\n![](images/7f/7fbfb3fd5bbacbf1c974bf654e993a7203934db5d679bfaa89ddc0c54e39a7df.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157354 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2981f6-bfbf-5c1e-a4a2-2814dc24804a" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Quadratic Function Where X Is a Function of Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dec569bc-4861-5f9b-9002-2902f4b4c77f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80dbbd79a79c59237d61ee228d47887187cb9856366686ce9520291f1d713e72.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156688} {:answer/id #uuid "e6afc5cb-aafa-572c-bf4f-2e18147ce5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95f55293ecb8a57ce34c50dfb11b5090923137273e4885e99bd54cae7b125e4f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156689} {:answer/id #uuid "075982d7-3367-5e34-a8c4-bb90d5e49ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/acafb0f5cec6fc2ad238fa9a1a53fee47fe8f0e37ded3c7733ec838a6c1d66e2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156690} {:answer/id #uuid "0a533d56-e848-502f-ba53-cd04f2196f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/af8a5de34c0cb4d24879c6dc211e8f610eab0a5602985ac82c43cd4db3c2d49e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156691} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3df525-d1dd-5895-9bfa-0e38c6d44d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/721db846a92d0ede38f6234154c54f55fe1bb3c5cae852e900864b1da1de2a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156692}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6cffed-a90f-54df-96b6-7b8eded745d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156687}] :question/id #uuid "803745d4-7e67-5cee-b697-645c72bb764f" :question/math-academy-id "q-88507" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x =-y^{2} - 3y$."}]}
